# Cached copies of bg3.wiki pages (~103 MB). Unlike the extracted facts in data/,
# these are wholesale copies of someone else's pages, so they stay local. Every
# script reads the cache when it is present and re-fetches politely when it is not.
cache/

# icons/ and assets/ are NOT ignored, on purpose.
#
# They used to be, because they are regenerable — which was right while this was a
# local-only tool. It stops being right once the site is published: a static host
# serves what the repo contains, so leaving them out would publish 1720 broken
# images. The alternative, re-fetching them in CI, would hit bg3.wiki on every
# single deploy for files that never change. Committing them once is both smaller
# on the wiki and simpler here: one repo, one deploy, nothing to rebuild.

# OS / editor noise
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini
.DS_Store
*.swp
*~
.vscode/
.idea/
